`merge_events(video, audio) -> tuple[tuple[int, object], ...]` merges two finite sequences of `(timestamp, payload)` pairs. A timestamp must be a nonnegative integer and not a boolean. Each input must already be ordered by nondecreasing timestamp. Malformed events or out-of-order inputs raise `ValueError`; empty inputs are valid.

Return all events in nondecreasing timestamp order. At equal timestamps, every video event must precede every audio event, while original order within each source is preserved. Deep-copy every payload in the result so mutable payloads share no aliases with either input or each other. Do not mutate either input.

